 {"id":"hero-noah","unit":"u1","hero":true,"price":0,"emoji":"🧓","hu":"Noé","en":"Noah","bio":{"hu":"Igaz ember volt, aki Istennel járt. Engedelmesen megépítette a bárkát, és Isten megmentette őt és családját az özönvízből.","en":"A righteous man who walked with God. He obediently built the ark, and God saved him and his family from the flood."}},
 {"id":"hero-abraham","unit":"u2","hero":true,"price":0,"emoji":"👴","hu":"Ábrahám","en":"Abraham","bio":{"hu":"Isten elhívta, hogy hagyja el hazáját. Hitt az ígéretben, hogy utódai annyian lesznek, mint az ég csillagai. A hit atyja.","en":"God called him to leave his homeland. He believed the promise that his descendants would be as many as the stars. The father of faith."}},
 {"id":"hero-moses","unit":"u3","hero":true,"price":0,"emoji":"🧔","hu":"Mózes","en":"Moses","bio":{"hu":"Isten az égő csipkebokornál hívta el. Kivezette Izráel népét Egyiptomból, és átvette a Tízparancsolatot a Sínai-hegyen.","en":"God called him at the burning bush. He led Israel out of Egypt and received the Ten Commandments on Mount Sinai."}},
 {"id":"hero-david","unit":"u4","hero":true,"price":0,"emoji":"🎯","hu":"Dávid","en":"David","bio":{"hu":"Pásztorfiúból lett Izráel királya. Parittyával győzte le Góliátot, és sok zsoltárt írt Isten dicséretére.","en":"From shepherd boy to king of Israel. He defeated Goliath with a sling and wrote many psalms in praise of God."}},
 {"id":"hero-peter","unit":"u5","hero":true,"price":0,"emoji":"🎣","hu":"Péter","en":"Peter","bio":{"hu":"Halász volt, akit Jézus tanítványul hívott. Bár megtagadta Jézust, bocsánatot kapott, és az egyház egyik vezetője lett.","en":"A fisherman whom Jesus called to be a disciple. Though he denied Jesus, he was forgiven and became a leader of the church."}},
 {"id":"hero-paul","unit":"u6","hero":true,"price":0,"emoji":"✍️","hu":"Pál","en":"Paul","bio":{"hu":"Először üldözte a keresztényeket, de a damaszkuszi úton találkozott Jézussal. Missziós utakon hirdette az evangéliumot, és leveleket írt a gyülekezeteknek.","en":"He first persecuted Christians, but met Jesus on the road to Damascus. He preached the gospel on missionary journeys and wrote letters to the churches."}}
